From 4e651587afd75366027c5b8db2db7bf4ac013a06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ho Cheung <hocheung@chromium.org>
Date: Tue, 08 Sep 2026 15:51:43 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [M153] Fix spurious resize events during webview autosizing

Original change's description:
> Fix spurious resize events during webview autosizing
>
> Scroll-width autosizing temporarily resizes a webview to measure
> narrower content. These internal sizes leaked resize notifications even
> when the stable viewport size was unchanged.
>
> Suppress resize notifications during internal measurements and report
> events and callbacks only when the stable size changes. Add coverage for
> fixed overlays and resize handlers that modify the DOM.
>
> Fixed: 555294645,555299651
> Change-Id: Ic8278dd93a63a08b26cf98f96f0b2ad50a6a6113
> Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8342172
> Reviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick <ikilpatrick@chromium.org>
> Commit-Queue: Aaron Teo <hocheung@chromium.org>
